# covers: 7 Memory exhaustion
# covers: 17 Resource exhaustion protection
# covers: 22 Memory exhaustion
# covers: 16 Resource limits
# covers: 22 Very large collections
# kind: edge
# expect: trap exceeded its capacity of 256 bytes

regionExhausted is module
regionExhausted purpose "Trap: a list that grows past its region's capacity"
regionExhausted path regionExhausted
regionExhausted imports standard.math
regionExhausted imports standard.compare
regionExhausted imports standard.list
regionExhausted exports main

Numbers is instance
Numbers purpose "A growable list of whole numbers"
Numbers instantiates list.List Int64

main is operation
main purpose "Run the case and print what it computes"
main invariant none
main typeParam none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwner none
main raises none
main effect none
main uses none
main memory heap true
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main label fill loopKind counted
main label fill within none
main label fill maxIterations 1000
main label fill counter index
main label appendStep loopKind none
main label appendStep within fill
main label done loopKind none
main label done within none
main let one immutable Int64 1
main let limit immutable Int64 1000
main let index mutable Int64 0
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main at begin do makeNumbers
main at begin goto fill
main at fill do filled
main at fill branch if isFilled goto done else goto appendStep
main at appendStep do appendIndex
main at appendStep do advance
main at appendStep set index nextIndex
main at appendStep goto fill
main at done return ok okCode

tiny is region
tiny in main
tiny strategy arena
tiny capacity 256
tiny released atReturn

makeNumbers is call
makeNumbers in main
makeNumbers invokes Numbers.new
makeNumbers arg region Region tiny lend
makeNumbers out numbers Numbers
makeNumbers ownedBy tiny
makeNumbers cleanedBy none
makeNumbers borrows none
makeNumbers catch none

filled is call
filled in main
filled invokes compare.greaterOrEqualInt64
filled arg left Int64 index copy
filled arg right Int64 limit copy
filled out isFilled Bool
filled ownedBy none
filled cleanedBy none
filled borrows none
filled catch none

appendIndex is call
appendIndex in main
appendIndex invokes Numbers.append
appendIndex arg list Numbers numbers lendMutable
appendIndex arg item Int64 index copy
appendIndex out none
appendIndex ownedBy none
appendIndex cleanedBy none
appendIndex borrows none
appendIndex catch none

advance is call
advance in main
advance invokes math.addInt64
advance arg left Int64 index copy
advance arg right Int64 one copy
advance out nextIndex Int64
advance ownedBy none
advance cleanedBy none
advance borrows none
advance catch none
